==Battleground==
*5 [[Shibalien Elite]]s spawn, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Kroxo]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Galactic Overseer Nyandam]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Kroxo]]s spawn, delay 4~10 seconds<sup>120f~300f</sup>.
**3 [[Cyberhorn]]s spawn, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
**3 [[Corporal Weyland]]s spawn, delay 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
**1 [[I.M. Phace]] spawns.
**3 [[Nimoy Bore]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
**3 [[Kid Tappa]]s spawn, delay 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
**5 [[Ribbo]]s spawn, delay 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Bring many [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] units and [[Barrier]] [[Barrier Breaker|Breakers]], such as [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]], [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]], [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]], [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]], etc. Remember to bring some [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]] or [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attack]] units because there are several backliners, such as Corporal Weyland. [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Golfer Cat]] is a good choice to break Ribbo's Barrier due to his Long Distance ability. Start stacking your golfers on the Shibalien Elites and the Kroxos in the beginning, before hitting the base.

